cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "When Does One-Step Endpoint Regression Preserve Conditional Spread? Coupling, Mean Dependence, and Data-Side Non-Identifiability"
abstract: >-
  Code and raw results for a study of when a one-step generative policy suffices.
  The paper defines the realised conditional-spread ratio rho, proves that rho of
  the L2-optimal one-step map is a property of the training target rather than of
  the data, gives a one-parameter family of training targets with an identical
  (c, x1) law for which rho sweeps [0, 1], and derives a minimax form showing that
  any data-only statistic has worst-case risk exactly 1/2. It also maps two escape
  channels and locates the loss channel's structure in the scope of the matching
  (pooled versus per-condition) rather than in the absence of a bijection.
